 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "관계대명사 who / which / that",
   "en": "relative pronouns who, which and that"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "who는 사람, which는 물건, that은 사람과 물건 둘 다 설명할 때 씁니다. 'He is the man who lives next door.'처럼 명사 뒤에 붙어 '~하는 …'이라는 뜻을 더합니다. who / which / that이 주어 역할을 하면 뒤에 다시 주어를 쓰지 않습니다.",
   "en": "Who is for people, which for things and that for both. They come after a noun and add information: He is the man who lives next door. When who / which / that is the subject, do not add another subject."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "who + 사람",
     "He is the man who lives next door."
    ],
    [
     "which + 물건",
     "This is a bag which I use every day."
    ],
    [
     "that + 둘 다",
     "It's a robot that cleans the room."
    ],
    [
     "직업 / job",
     "He is a chef who makes Italian food."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "사람 = who (또는 that), 물건 = which (또는 that).",
    "en": "People = who (or that); things = which (or that)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "who / which / that 뒤에는 동사 (주어 역할).",
    "en": "After who / which / that comes a verb (it is the subject)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "회화에서는 that을 자주 씁니다.",
    "en": "In speech that is very common."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
